WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:02.670
- [Mark] Regina, so where'd you grow up?

00:00:02.670 --> 00:00:04.564
- I grew up in the Nickerson Gardens.

00:00:04.564 --> 00:00:05.397
- [Mark] Which is the?

00:00:05.397 --> 00:00:08.033
- [Regina] Which is the
projects and the Bounty Hunters.

00:00:08.897 --> 00:00:10.530
I was a runaway.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.920
I left my family 'cause I was hot headed.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:13.753
- [Mark] At what age?

00:00:13.753 --> 00:00:14.586
- [Regina] At 12.

00:00:14.586 --> 00:00:16.360
- [Mark] At 12? Wow.

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:19.483
- Yeah, and I started
drinking, and partying,

00:00:20.524 --> 00:00:21.693
and mixing.

00:00:23.853 --> 00:00:26.126
I started doing things that wasn't...

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.294
That I didn't grew up...

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.140
That I knew better than doing.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.382
But eventually, the fight
started coming because

00:00:32.382 --> 00:00:34.350
I was young and girls was jealous

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:35.590
because I was younger than them,

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:36.887
and I was prettier than them.

00:00:36.887 --> 00:00:38.540
Or because I had more attention.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:41.460
But then, I think I liked it that

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.450
I had to start fighting,

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.523
because it made me,

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:46.720
who I am today.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.070
My struggle made me strong.

00:00:49.073 --> 00:00:49.906
- [Mark] What...

00:00:49.906 --> 00:00:50.739
So, you've done prison time?

00:00:50.739 --> 00:00:51.572
- I've been imprisoned-

00:00:51.572 --> 00:00:53.090
I went to prison at the age of 18.

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:56.910
I escaped from Sybil Brand
1995. October 1st, 1995.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:57.743
I was the first...

00:00:57.743 --> 00:00:58.900
Me and Rebecca Dahl was the

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:01.940
first two individuals to
ever escape Sybil Brand.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:02.990
It was scaring me.

00:01:02.990 --> 00:01:04.150
I didn't know nothing about prison.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:05.890
I thought I would to go to
prison and be somebody bitch.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.924
So, I escaped from Sybil Brand.

00:01:07.924 --> 00:01:08.757
- [Mark] Wait. What is Sybil Brand?

00:01:08.757 --> 00:01:10.210
- It's the county jail for women.

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:11.043
- [Mark] Oh, I see.

00:01:11.043 --> 00:01:12.300
- It was on the news. If you
Google it, you would see.

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.592
- [Mark] So you escaped from prison?

00:01:13.592 --> 00:01:14.425
- Yeah, I escaped from there.

00:01:14.425 --> 00:01:15.682
I was on the news.

00:01:15.682 --> 00:01:18.127
America's most wanted.
You know the features:

00:01:18.127 --> 00:01:19.640
"Have you seen this person?"

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.750
They caught me 32 days later.

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.380
They caught her the next day.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:25.453
I did my first prison term at 18.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:27.550
I'm 42 years old.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.810
I've got, no, I don't have 10.

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:32.320
I have 13 prison terms.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.233
One strike.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.120
I be down here since I was 13.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:38.403
I've worked the streets.

00:01:40.452 --> 00:01:44.000
I've done a little bit
of everything down here.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.660
- [Mark] Tell me about
you parents, growing up.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:47.700
- My parents, my mother was a addict,

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.110
and my dad, I stayed with my dad,

00:01:49.110 --> 00:01:51.130
but I always wanted my mom.

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:52.880
But my mom was on her drugs and stuff.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.110
And the last time I remember having my mom

00:01:55.110 --> 00:02:00.110
when she was on the patio
naked, she was on her PCP.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:01.500
And she had a trick down on her throat.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.160
She couldn't talk.

00:02:03.160 --> 00:02:04.903
And my dad took me from her,

00:02:05.814 --> 00:02:06.647
and my dad,

00:02:06.647 --> 00:02:07.480
he was a (stutters).

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.490
He was a addict himself,

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.643
but he was more a functional addict.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:13.280
But then things got out of hand

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:16.280
and him and his current wife got into it,

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.380
so he left me with my grandmother.

00:02:18.380 --> 00:02:20.180
My grandmother was a church goer, so

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.060
she didn't keep up with me that much.

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:24.893
She just-

00:02:24.893 --> 00:02:26.070
I just did what I wanted to do.

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:27.653
You know, disregard her.

00:02:30.131 --> 00:02:32.381
But yeah, I would find
myself on the streets.

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:34.640
After the gang bang, that's when

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.040
I left Nickerson Garden
because it got too much.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.720
I headed to Bill Barton's.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.340
I started working the
streets at Bill Barton's

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.243
at the age of 14.

00:02:43.984 --> 00:02:45.200
And I raped.

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.010
I remember getting raped.

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:50.700
And um, that slowed- (knocking).

00:02:50.700 --> 00:02:52.720
That slowed me down a little bit.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.350
I eventually got with somebody older.

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:55.183
He was things,

00:02:55.183 --> 00:02:56.360
Norman Boosac.

00:02:56.360 --> 00:02:59.250
He was 40, I was 15,

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.570
and we came down here and
that's when I started...

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.640
Came down here and I started selling drugs

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:05.870
and gang-banging more.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.120
And then we went back to Compton.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.110
That's when I became...

00:03:08.110 --> 00:03:10.330
I'm from South side, I'm actually a Crip.

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:12.090
I grew up with the Bloods but I...

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.760
So then I started selling drugs down here.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:16.930
When I started selling drugs down here,

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.660
I was making lots of money.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.690
I was making so much money,

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:22.630
but my mother ended up dying.

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:23.463
When mother ended up dying,

00:03:23.463 --> 00:03:25.313
I ended up, started using cocaine.

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.783
- [Mark] So you were
selling but not using?

00:03:27.783 --> 00:03:28.745
- I was selling but not using.

00:03:28.745 --> 00:03:29.578
When I was younger,

00:03:29.578 --> 00:03:31.790
I was smoking weed, PCP, but never crack.

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.390
I started excusing last,
to became my best customer.

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.785
- [Mark] You became your best customer?

00:03:36.785 --> 00:03:37.865
- (laughs)

00:03:37.865 --> 00:03:39.573
I became my best customer.

00:03:40.942 --> 00:03:42.310
I ended up losing a lot of people

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:43.910
I thought meant something to me,

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:46.550
but I didn't care. My mother was gone.

00:03:46.550 --> 00:03:47.550
I wanted to be numb.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:51.303
Started working the streets again.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:57.450
(indistinct background noise)

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.387
And my...

00:03:58.387 --> 00:03:59.220
And I started...

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.090
I started changing because Downtown you.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:03.920
People bring things out of you

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:04.780
that you don't want to...

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.463
That you didn't know that was there.

00:04:08.561 --> 00:04:10.660
(indistinct background chattering)

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.983
This got me thinking. (laughs)

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:15.100
Next question.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.970
- [Mark] Living Downtown's
a trip, isn't it?

00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:17.880
- Downtown is...

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:21.119
It's actually I've been down here...

00:04:21.119 --> 00:04:23.152
14. I've been down here almost 30 years.

00:04:23.152 --> 00:04:24.430
- [Mark] 30 years?

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.690
What's the craziest thing
you've seen down here?

00:04:25.690 --> 00:04:28.030
- The craziest thing I've
seen when I seen a woman

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.780
get pushed out the frontier window.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:32.570
I seen a woman, two people actually.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:33.530
The frontier.

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:35.860
I was outside hustling.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:36.809
- [Mark] Which floor?

00:04:36.809 --> 00:04:37.642
- I don't know what floor she came from

00:04:37.642 --> 00:04:38.475
but she came...

00:04:38.475 --> 00:04:40.760
Cause I was outside and it was like, bam.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.460
I've never seen nothing like that.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.193
I was in the Cecil and the girl,

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:48.830
she jumped, she jumped.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.663
They say she jumped

00:04:49.663 --> 00:04:52.083
but I don't think she jumped. Room 742.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.190
She fell but she lived.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.140
- [Mark] She lived?

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.230
- She lived for two days

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.270
and when she turned
herself she could fell.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.570
And when she fell, she turned herself

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.407
over and she was saying, "Please, Lord.

00:05:02.407 --> 00:05:03.470
Please don't let me die.

00:05:03.470 --> 00:05:05.463
Please let me live long." Tell him.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.153
I don't know if she...

00:05:07.153 --> 00:05:08.990
I think she may have told
it, but she ended up dying.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.600
But she lived two days after the seventh.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:11.433
The Cecil.

00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:13.708
I don't know if you know where
to stay in on maintenance.

00:05:13.708 --> 00:05:15.365
That seventh floor is high.

00:05:15.365 --> 00:05:16.198
- [Mark] Very.

00:05:16.198 --> 00:05:19.078
- Yeah. That was one of the
craziest things I've seen.

00:05:19.078 --> 00:05:19.911
- [Mark] (indistinct)

00:05:19.911 --> 00:05:21.110
No, not actually.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:22.590
The man that got caught on fire.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.010
That set on fire not too long ago.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.910
That was the craziest thing I've seen.

00:05:27.689 --> 00:05:28.522
Yeah.

00:05:28.522 --> 00:05:29.796
- [Mark] You've seen it all.

00:05:29.796 --> 00:05:31.419
- (laughs) I haven't seen...

00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:32.252
I've seen enough.

00:05:32.252 --> 00:05:33.237
- [Mark] Do you have kids of your own?

00:05:33.237 --> 00:05:34.590
- I have seven kids.

00:05:34.590 --> 00:05:35.520
- [Mark] Seven kids?

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:36.900
- I have.

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:38.070
I didn't become a mother until I had

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.083
my last baby boy.

00:05:40.083 --> 00:05:43.233
I've had drug-related babies.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:47.403
My daughter, she won a
scholarship for Beating The Odds.

00:05:47.403 --> 00:05:48.410
She's...

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.950
She's a nurse now.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.540
She graduated St. Mary's.

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.820
She's the best part of me.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.970
She overcame all this,
her mama leaving her.

00:05:55.970 --> 00:05:58.360
I left her in the hospital
when she a preemie

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.850
to go get high.

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.050
I had the staples in my
stomach and I left the hospital

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:04.257
with staples in my stomach to
come down here and get high.

00:06:04.257 --> 00:06:06.730
And my baby wasn't doing better.

00:06:07.587 --> 00:06:09.090
But I have seven kids

00:06:11.833 --> 00:06:13.433
and I want another one actually.

00:06:14.288 --> 00:06:16.170
- [Mark] But the last one you're raising?

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:17.090
- The last one I'm raising,

00:06:17.090 --> 00:06:18.310
but right now he stays with my cousin

00:06:18.310 --> 00:06:20.850
because I had went to prison
and I had my son with me.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:22.440
That's the only one I raised,

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:24.870
but I went to prison for sales

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:25.703
and my cousin...

00:06:25.703 --> 00:06:28.880
I gave my cousin temporary guardianship

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.830
and I don't want him back down here, so

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.810
I'm trying to get me together
so I can get my baby back.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:37.572
I've been clean for
five months, three days.

00:06:37.572 --> 00:06:38.840
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:39.810
How do you...

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:42.980
how do you get clean from crack?

00:06:42.980 --> 00:06:45.520
- I got clean from crack
by smoking crystal.

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:46.660
I weighed myself off crack.

00:06:46.660 --> 00:06:47.750
- [Mark] I've been through that before.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:48.839
- I did that.

00:06:48.839 --> 00:06:50.570
And then now I don't smoke.

00:06:50.570 --> 00:06:51.693
I don't have the taste for crystal no more

00:06:51.693 --> 00:06:53.480
because I look at everybody and they start

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.660
picking their face.

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:57.600
I see certain people and they're...

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:00.100
They're delusional and
I don't want to be that.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:00.933
I've been...

00:07:00.933 --> 00:07:03.010
I've done a lot out here and I want...

00:07:03.010 --> 00:07:04.780
I thank God that my brain is still

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.129
somewhat.

00:07:07.129 --> 00:07:07.962
- [Mark] (giggles) Exactly.

00:07:07.962 --> 00:07:09.360
- So I just take one day at a time.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:11.810
I'll say today, just for
today, I won't get high.

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:13.530
So tomorrow when I wake up

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:14.590
I'll say just for today, I won't get high.

00:07:14.590 --> 00:07:16.460
- [Mark] That's very good.

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:17.293
- So...

00:07:17.293 --> 00:07:18.126
- [Mark] Good for you.

00:07:18.126 --> 00:07:19.627
- Yeah.

00:07:19.627 --> 00:07:20.547
- [Mark] That's great.

00:07:20.547 --> 00:07:21.508
That's nice to hear.

00:07:21.508 --> 00:07:22.341
- Yeah.

00:07:22.341 --> 00:07:23.580
- [Mark] That's rare.

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:25.040
- Yeah. I've gone through a time

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.260
in my life where I down here,
I've lost my baby thought...

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.550
People think that I had
told on somebody down here.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.410
So it's like...

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:33.930
But where I come from,

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.950
you're not supposed to...

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.730
You're supposed to have
proof on something like that

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:39.560
instead of just put a pin in that on down.

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.530
So I had to go prove
myself to a lot of people

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:43.710
that I didn't do what they thought I did.

00:07:43.710 --> 00:07:44.640
And it made me realize

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.150
that they was never my friend
at all in the first place.

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:48.400
So I'm separating myself.

00:07:50.220 --> 00:07:53.660
- [Mark] So your kids,
how many different dads?

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:56.495
- Oh, all of them have different dads.

00:07:56.495 --> 00:07:57.626
- [Mark] Seven kids, seven dads.

00:07:57.626 --> 00:07:59.878
- I have seven...

00:07:59.878 --> 00:08:01.585
Six baby daddies, seven kids.

00:08:01.585 --> 00:08:03.861
I have a set of twins.

00:08:03.861 --> 00:08:05.108
I have...

00:08:05.108 --> 00:08:06.317
And actually...

00:08:06.317 --> 00:08:09.510
Actually my son, my last
baby, his dad is in prison.

00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:13.410
And my husband, I had met, we
got married three years ago.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.910
He's in prison right now.

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:16.750
He helped me raise my son.

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.750
He'd adopted my son.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:19.820
They tried to take my baby

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:20.840
and everything when I was in prison.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:23.440
But he put a stop to that.

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.763
His name is Life, my baby.

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:28.667
I have, yeah, a lot of baby daddies.

00:08:28.667 --> 00:08:29.500
Probably would have more kids.

00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:30.610
I've had two abortions.

00:08:31.957 --> 00:08:33.740
- [Mark] What are your kids' names?

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.796
- Christopher is 26.

00:08:35.796 --> 00:08:36.629
Ronisha's 24. She'll be 25.

00:08:38.707 --> 00:08:39.960
Reality is 19.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.040
Forever is 17.

00:08:42.040 --> 00:08:45.086
Asia and Isaiah is 15.

00:08:45.086 --> 00:08:48.710
Amira is 12 and...

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.440
No, Amira's 13.

00:08:50.440 --> 00:08:52.363
And Life is six.

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:56.550
- [Mark] What would you say to them

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.070
if you could talk to
them, all (indistinct).

00:08:58.070 --> 00:08:59.510
- If I could tell them right now,

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:01.680
I would tell them I apologize for

00:09:05.840 --> 00:09:07.435
not being there for you.

00:09:07.435 --> 00:09:09.250
For missing out on all the time that

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.550
you needed me to be there.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:17.643
If it's not too late, I
hope we can be friends.

00:09:19.060 --> 00:09:20.210
Get to know each other.

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:22.444
It's not a day that goes by that

00:09:22.444 --> 00:09:24.694
I don't think of you
and wonder how you look.

00:09:27.576 --> 00:09:30.477
I wonder if you thinking of me
like I'm thinking about you.

00:09:31.840 --> 00:09:33.100
But I never forget you a smile.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:34.260
I never forget your smell.

00:09:34.260 --> 00:09:35.093
I always...

00:09:35.093 --> 00:09:38.050
I love to smell my babies
when they was born,

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:40.377
but I love you guys.

00:09:40.377 --> 00:09:42.044
And hopefully we can

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.022
